      "math_academy_id": "q-85435",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $26\\,489\\,225$\n\nII. $14\\,736\\,438$\n\nIII. $749\\,356\\,314$",
      "worked_solution": "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$\n\n- The number $26\\,489\\,225$ is not divisible by $2,$ so it is not divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- The number $14\\,736\\,438$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+4+7+3+6+4+3+8=36\n$$\n\nSo, $14\\,736\\,438$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $749\\,356\\,314$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n7+4+9+3+5+6+3+1+4=42\n$$\n\nSo, $749\\,356\\,314$ is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
